An sret (> 16-byte) value receiver from a call/temp is captured via an OP_CALL result backend-represented as a POINTER to the sret buffer (not an OP_ALLOC), so it can be neither load-then-stored nor stored directly into the by-value closure field (`'%v0' type 'ptr' but expected %Big`).  The register-returned capture (947/949) is gated to !NeedsSret; the sret case stays the old dangling-`*Big` crash.  Fix: sret destination-forwarding into the closure field, or a backend-aware struct-copy.  Tracked in claude-todo.md.
